+The norm check of D fails when any one batch's ``norm_error`` reaches the same limit ``hipblaslt-test`` uses for the GEMM. The limit is the largest tolerance among the output and both input types (1e-5 for f32, 0.01 for f16, 0.1 for bf16); f32 output with ``c_f32_fast_bf16_r`` uses at least 0.5. For example, f16 inputs with f32 output use 0.01. The bench then prints the failing batch and its error to stderr. By default the exit code is 0 whether or not a check fails. With ``--verify_strict``, the bench exits with code 2 when any check of D failed. Only the first launch of each solution is compared with the reference; the launches timed by ``--iters`` and ``--cold_iters`` are not checked.
 
